          "summaryEn": "DIVIDE expressions allow you to understand and use both divide 48 by 6 and divide 6 into 48 correctly. Divide something up helps you explain how something is shared fairly between or among people. Divide up into can describe students forming teams, guests forming lines or something being separated into smaller parts. Divide something off can describe how a curtain, wall, screen or fence separates one area from another.",
