        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "用 HAND 清楚交接發言次序",
            "titleEn": "Use HAND to manage speaking turns clearly",
            "zh": "hand over 和 hand somebody back 可以幫助講者、主持人和記者,把節目或討論順暢地交給另一人。",
            "en": "Hand over and hand somebody back help speakers, presenters and reporters pass a programme or discussion smoothly from one person to another."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論責任和控制權的轉交",
            "titleEn": "Talk about responsibility and control",
            "zh": "hand over 可以表示把項目、店舖或工作交給另一人管理。",
            "en": "Hand over can describe giving a project, shop or job to another person to manage."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "清楚表達不同的交付方式",
            "titleEn": "Show different ways of giving things",
            "zh": "hand in 表示提交;hand back 表示歸還;hand on 表示傳給下一個人;hand round 表示逐一傳給所有人。",
            "en": "Hand in means submit, hand back means return, hand on means pass to the next person, and hand round means pass to everyone."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論家族物品和傳統",
            "titleEn": "Talk about family items and traditions",
            "zh": "hand down 可以描述衣物、物件、食譜、歌曲或故事由年長家人傳給年輕一代。",
            "en": "Hand down describes clothes, objects, recipes, songs or stories passing from older family members to younger ones."
          }
        ],
