          "labelEn": "WALK Phrasal Verbs in Use",
          "summaryZh": "walk away、walk off 和 walk out 可以表達不同的離開原因和方式。；walk off with a prize 表示輕易得獎;walk off with somebody’s phone 則表示未經許可拿走別人的電話。；你可以分辨撞上門、跌入圈套,以及走近某人等不同情況。；你可以用 walk through a scene 表示簡單排練,也可以用 walk somebody through a process 表示逐步講解流程。",
          "summaryEn": "movement Walk away, walk off and walk out express different reasons and ways of leaving. Walk off with a prize means winning it easily, but walk off with somebody’s phone means taking it without permission. You can distinguish walking into a door, walking into a trap and walking up to a person. You can walk through a scene during a simple rehearsal or walk somebody through a process by explaining each stage.",
