          "variableEn": "Keep the same people, things, time and meaning. Test somebody out and test something out are complete expressions. With him, her, it or them, place the word between TEST and OUT: test him out test it out Extra parts such as during a shift, on a class or by giving somebody a task only add details. They are not fixed parts of the expression. Use test for something when the person or thing being checked is not named. Use test somebody/something for something when it is named. They are testing for oil. They tested the water for lead.",
