        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "清楚表達延誤由誰或甚麼造成",
            "titleEn": "Show who or what causes a delay",
            "zh": "drag on 表示事情本身持續得太久;drag something out 則表示某人或某個行動令事情持續得太久。",
            "en": "Drag on describes something that continues for too long. Drag something out shows that a person or action makes it last too long."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "描述不情願地被帶走或捨不得離開",
            "titleEn": "Describe unwilling movement or difficulty leaving",
            "zh": "drag somebody off 可以表示某人不情願地被帶走;drag yourself away 可以表示自己捨不得停止一項喜歡的活動。",
            "en": "Drag somebody off can show that a person is made to go somewhere unwillingly. Drag yourself away can show that you find it difficult to stop an enjoyable activity."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "表達不必要的牽涉和負面影響",
            "titleEn": "Explain unwanted involvement and harmful effects",
            "zh": "drag somebody in 或 drag somebody into something 可以描述某人被牽涉進事情;dragsomebody or something down 則可以描述情緒、行為、質素或表現受到拖累。",
            "en": "Drag somebody in or into something describes unwanted involvement. Drag somebody or something down describes a harmful effect on mood, behaviour, quality or performance."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論舊問題再次被提起",
            "titleEn": "Talk about old problems returning",
            "zh": "當某人重提過去、尷尬或令人不快的事情時,可以使用 drag something up。",
            "en": "Drag something up is useful when somebody mentions an old, embarrassing or unpleasant subject again."
          }
        ],
