          "incorrectForms": [],
          "variableZh": "保留原句中的人物、事物、時間和意思。；相近的表達可以有不同意思。例如,fall off 可以表示「下降」,也可以表示「脫落」。fall in 和 falldown 都可以描述倒塌,但方式不同。；on 和 upon 有時可以表達相同意思;with 和 in 亦會按參考表所示的形式使用。",
          "variableEn": "Keep the same people, things, time and meaning. Similar expressions may have different meanings. For example, fall off can mean “decrease” or “become detached”. Fall in and fall down both describe collapse, but in different ways. On and upon can sometimes express the same meaning. With and in are both used in the forms shown in the reference bank.",
