          "summaryEn": "SWEEP expressions can distinguish between cleaning a whole room, collecting dirt and removing something from a surface. Sweep somebody along or away can describe being strongly affected by an atmosphere, while sweep somebody off their feet describes suddenly falling deeply in love. SWEEP can describe a team defeating an opponent easily, a flood carrying something away or a person refusing to consider an objection. These expressions often appear in conversations, stories, sports reports and descriptions of storms or floods.",
