        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "以不同方式詢問某人的情況",
            "titleEn": "Ask about people in different ways",
            "zh": "ask after somebody 可以用來問候某人;ask for somebody 則可以表示要求與某人交談。",
            "en": "Ask after somebody lets you enquire about a person’s wellbeing, while ask for somebody lets you request to speak to that person."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "提出要求並尋找有用資料",
            "titleEn": "Request things and find useful information",
            "zh": "ask for something 可以表示索取所需的事物;ask around 則可以表示向多人打聽資料。",
            "en": "Ask for something lets you request what you need. Ask around helps you obtain information from several people."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "更準確地提出邀請",
            "titleEn": "Make invitations more precisely",
            "zh": "ASK 片語動詞可以清楚表示某人是同行、進入房間、到你家作客,還是活動後跟你回去。",
            "en": "ASK expressions can show whether someone is joining your activity, entering a room, visiting your home or returning with you after an event."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "理解不同社交邀請的分別",
            "titleEn": "Understand important social differences",
            "zh": "ask somebody along、ask somebody round 和 ask somebody out 表示不同類型的邀請。選用正確表達,可以令意思更清楚。",
            "en": "Ask somebody along, ask somebody round and ask somebody out describe different kinds of invitations. Choosing the correct one makes your meaning much clearer."
          }
        ],
