          {
            "titleZh": "清楚表達不同的清潔工作",
            "titleEn": "Talk clearly about different cleaning jobs",
            "zh": "wipe down 表示清潔整個表面;wipe off 則表示擦掉某一處污漬或物質。",
            "en": "Wipe down describes cleaning a whole surface, while wipe off describes removing a particular mark or substance."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "自然談論濺瀉物和廚房工作",
            "titleEn": "Handle spills and kitchen jobs naturally",
            "zh": "你可以用 wipe something up 表示抹走濺出的飲品,也可以在英式英語中用 wipe up 表示把洗好的餐具抹乾。",
            "en": "You can wipe up spilled drinks and use wipe up in British English when drying washed dishes."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "更容易理解運動英語",
            "titleEn": "Understand sports English more easily",
            "zh": "wipe out 可以表示某人從滑浪板或滑板上跌倒,也可以表示一支球隊以大比數擊敗對手。",
            "en": "Wipe out may describe someone falling from a surfboard or skateboard, or a team winning by a very large score."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "表達徹底清除或摧毀",
            "titleEn": "Describe complete removal or destruction",
            "zh": "wipe something out 表示某事物被完全或幾乎完全消滅。",
            "en": "Wipe something out shows that nothing, or almost nothing, remains."
          }
