        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "使用 HANG 談論等候和空閒時間",
            "titleEn": "Use HANG to talk about waiting and free time",
            "zh": "hang around 和 hang about 可以描述在某處等候或逗留;hang out 和 hang with 則可以描述與其他人一起消磨時間。",
            "en": "Hang around and hang about can describe waiting or staying somewhere. Hang out and hang with can describe spending time with other people."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "解釋結果取決於甚麼,以及哪些憂慮仍然存在",
            "titleEn": "Explain what a result depends on and what worry remains",
            "zh": "hang on 可以表示某個結果或決定取決於某事;hang over 則可以表示某種憂慮或危險仍未消失。",
            "en": "Hang on can show that a result or decision depends on something. Hang over can show that a worry or danger has not gone away."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "掌握 HANG ON TO 的兩個實用意思",
            "titleEn": "Show two useful meanings of HANG ON TO",
            "zh": "你可以 hang on to a receipt,表示保留收據;也可以 hang on to a rail,表示緊緊抓住扶手。",
            "en": "You can hang on to a receipt because you want to keep it, or hang on to a rail because you need to hold it tightly."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論責任,以及不同內容是否前後一致",
            "titleEn": "Talk about blame and whether ideas make sense",
            "zh": "hang something on somebody 可以描述把責任歸咎於某人;hang together 則可以描述故事、計劃或解釋整體上是否合理連貫。",
            "en": "Hang something on somebody describes blaming someone. Hang together describes a story, plan or explanation that makes sense as a whole."
          }
        ],
