          {
            "titleZh": "清楚描述放置和排列物件",
            "titleEn": "Talk clearly about placing and arranging things",
            "zh": "LAY 片語動詞能幫助你分辨把東西放到一旁、放下,以及攤開排列供人觀看等不同動作。",
            "en": "LAY expressions help you distinguish between putting something to one side, placing it down and arranging it for people to see."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論為日後作準備",
            "titleEn": "Talk about preparation for later",
            "zh": "你可以用 lay something by 和 lay something in 表示留起或儲備物資,也可以用 lay somethingon 表示安排服務或活動。",
            "en": "You can use lay something by and lay something in for saving or preparing supplies, and lay something on for arranging a service or event."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "描述工作、健康和交通情況",
            "titleEn": "Describe work, health and transport situations",
            "zh": "LAY 片語動詞可以描述解僱員工、因傷病而無法工作,以及讓船隻暫停使用。",
            "en": "The LAY family can describe dismissing workers, being unable to work because of illness, and taking a boat out of use."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "理解強烈警告和批評",
            "titleEn": "Understand strong warnings and criticism",
            "zh": "lay off 和 lay into 等表達常見於警告、批評或憤怒說話的情境。認識它們有助你理解說話者的態度。",
            "en": "Expressions such as lay off and lay into often appear when people are warning, criticising or speaking angrily. Recognising them helps you understand the speaker’s attitude."
          }
