          "summaryZh": "live by、live off 和 live on 可以說明某人靠一項活動賺錢、依靠別人供養,或靠某筆收入生活。；live in、live out 和 live with 可以說明某人住在工作地點、住在外面,或與另一個人同住。；live by 可以描述奉行的原則;live for 可以表示生命中最重要的事;live with 則可以描述接受不理想的情況。；live through、live out、live on、live something down 和 live up to 可以用來談論重大經歷、夢想、回憶、尷尬事情和期望。",
          "summaryEn": "Live by, live off and live on help you explain whether someone earns money through an activity, depends on another person or manages with a particular income. Live in, live out and live with help you explain whether someone stays at a workplace, lives elsewhere or shares a home with another person. Live by describes a guiding principle, live for shows what matters most to someone, and live with describes accepting something unpleasant. Live through, live out, live on, live something down and live up to help you discuss major experiences, dreams, memories, embarrassment and expectations.",
