          "summaryZh": "give in 表示停止抵抗;give up 表示停止某項活動或嘗試;give up on somebody/something 則表示不再相信某人或某事能成功。；你可以 give of your time,表示付出時間;give something back,表示歸還物件;give somethingaway,表示送出物件;give something out,則表示派發物品。；give off 可以描述熱力、光或氣味;give onto 可以描述門窗通往哪裏;give out 則可以表示電池、聲音或供應停止運作。；give somebody away 可以表示暴露秘密,也可以用於婚禮情境;give something over 表示轉交控制權或使用權;give yourself up 則表示投降。",
          "summaryEn": "Give in describes stopping your resistance. Give up describes stopping an activity or attempt, while give up on somebody or something shows that you no longer expect success. You can give of your time, give an object back, give unwanted things away or give papers out to a group. Give off can describe heat, light or smells. Give onto describes where a door or window leads, while give out can show that a battery, voice or supply has stopped working. Give somebody away can reveal a secret or have a special wedding meaning. Give something over transfers its control or use, while give yourself up describes surrendering.",
