          {
            "titleZh": "使用 GET 清楚描述旅程和移動",
            "titleEn": "Use GET to describe travel and movement clearly",
            "zh": "get over、get past 和 get out 可以描述前往某地、越過狹窄位置,以及安全離開某個地方。",
            "en": "Get over, get past and get out help you describe travelling somewhere, moving through a narrow space and leaving a place safely."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "自然談論復原和信心",
            "titleEn": "Talk naturally about recovery and confidence",
            "zh": "get over 可以描述從疾病或失望中恢復,也可以表示克服恐懼或害羞。",
            "en": "Get over can describe recovering from an illness or disappointment, as well as overcoming fear or shyness."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "運用 GET 處理日常安排",
            "titleEn": "Handle everyday arrangements with useful GET expressions",
            "zh": "你可以用 GET 表達請水喉匠前來、送孩子上學、請教練回來,或介紹某人使用實用的應用程式。",
            "en": "You can get a plumber in, get the children off to school, get a coach back or get somebody onto a useful app."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "表達延遲處理的事情和無法迴避的問題",
            "titleEn": "Express delayed tasks and unavoidable problems",
            "zh": "get round to 表示拖延後終於做某事;get round something 則表示避開或處理障礙。",
            "en": "Get round to shows that you finally do something after a delay. Get round something shows that you avoid or deal with an obstacle."
          }
