        "register": {
          "labelZh": "KNOCK 片語動詞的實際用途",
          "labelEn": "KNOCK Phrasal Verbs in Use",
          "summaryZh": "knock about 或 knock around 可以表示與某人來往、在某地四處遊歷,或某物長時間隨處放着。；KNOCK 片語動詞可以描述某人跌倒、失去知覺、被撞離單車,也可以表示物件被碰翻、撞壞或敲進某處。；你可以用 knock off 表示下班、knock somebody back 表示花費、knock something off a price 表示減價,以及 knock somebody down 表示議價。；KNOCK 可以表示迅速喝下飲品、迅速完成作品、迅速做成某物,或在網球比賽前擊球熱身。；knock it off 用來叫某人停止;knock yourself out 則表示對方可以儘管去做。",
          "summaryEn": "Knock about or knock around can describe spending time with people, travelling through places or things that have been lying unused for a long time. KNOCK expressions can show a person falling, becoming unconscious, being forced off a bicycle, or an object being tipped over, broken or driven into a surface. You can use knock off for finishing work, knock somebody back for cost, knock something off a price for a reduction and knock somebody down when bargaining. KNOCK can describe drinking something quickly, producing a piece of work quickly, making something quickly or warming up before a tennis match. Knock it off tells somebody to stop. Knock yourself out tells somebody they may go ahead and do as much as they like.",
          "contextsZh": [
            "用 KNOCK 談論人物、地方和物件的不同狀況",
            "更準確描述碰撞和移動",
            "自然談論工作、價錢和花費",
            "用同一系列表達多種迅速完成的動作",
            "理解有力的非正式命令和許可"
          ],
          "contextsEn": [
            "Use KNOCK to talk about people, places and things in different ways",
            "Describe impacts and movement more precisely",
            "Talk naturally about work, prices and costs",
            "Express quick actions with one family of verbs",
            "Understand strong informal commands and permission"
          ],
          "formalZh": "閱讀整句,選出意思相同的 KNOCK 片語動詞。",
          "formalEn": "Read the whole sentence and choose the KNOCK expression that gives the same meaning."
        },
