        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "用 KNOCK 談論人物、地方和物件的不同狀況",
            "titleEn": "Use KNOCK to talk about people, places and things in different ways",
            "zh": "knock about 或 knock around 可以表示與某人來往、在某地四處遊歷,或某物長時間隨處放着。",
            "en": "Knock about or knock around can describe spending time with people, travelling through places or things that have been lying unused for a long time."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "更準確描述碰撞和移動",
            "titleEn": "Describe impacts and movement more precisely",
            "zh": "KNOCK 片語動詞可以描述某人跌倒、失去知覺、被撞離單車,也可以表示物件被碰翻、撞壞或敲進某處。",
            "en": "KNOCK expressions can show a person falling, becoming unconscious, being forced off a bicycle, or an object being tipped over, broken or driven into a surface."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "自然談論工作、價錢和花費",
            "titleEn": "Talk naturally about work, prices and costs",
            "zh": "你可以用 knock off 表示下班、knock somebody back 表示花費、knock something off a price 表示減價,以及 knock somebody down 表示議價。",
            "en": "You can use knock off for finishing work, knock somebody back for cost, knock something off a price for a reduction and knock somebody down when bargaining."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "用同一系列表達多種迅速完成的動作",
            "titleEn": "Express quick actions with one family of verbs",
            "zh": "KNOCK 可以表示迅速喝下飲品、迅速完成作品、迅速做成某物,或在網球比賽前擊球熱身。",
            "en": "KNOCK can describe drinking something quickly, producing a piece of work quickly, making something quickly or warming up before a tennis match."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "理解有力的非正式命令和許可",
            "titleEn": "Understand strong informal commands and permission",
            "zh": "knock it off 用來叫某人停止;knock yourself out 則表示對方可以儘管去做。",
            "en": "Knock it off tells somebody to stop. Knock yourself out tells somebody they may go ahead and do as much as they like."
          }
        ],
