        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "談論擴建建築物",
            "titleEn": "Talk about making buildings larger",
            "zh": "add on 和 add on to something 可以表示在原有建築物上加建,而不需要搬到另一座建築物。",
            "en": "Add on and add on to something let you explain that an extra part is being built without moving to another building."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "清楚說明額外價錢和費用",
            "titleEn": "Explain extra prices and costs clearly",
            "zh": "add something in 可以表示把費用包括在計算內;add something on 則可以表示在原有價錢上再加收費用。",
            "en": "Add something in can show that a cost is included in a calculation. Add something on can show that an extra charge is placed on an existing price."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論總數和共同造成的結果",
            "titleEn": "Talk about totals and combined results",
            "zh": "你可以把數字加起來,也可以表示多項因素共同造成某個結果,或說明多筆款項合計為某個總額。",
            "en": "You can add numbers together, explain that several things added together to create a result, or say that amounts add up to a total."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "判斷資料是否合理",
            "titleEn": "Question whether information is logical",
            "zh": "add up 可以自然地表示某個說法、解釋、日期或一組數字是否合理。",
            "en": "Add up is a natural way to say that a story, explanation, date or set of numbers does or does not make sense."
          }
        ],
