        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "使用 SCREW 描述物件如何固定或接合",
            "titleEn": "Use SCREW to describe how things are fixed together",
            "zh": "screw down、screw on 和 screw onto 可以幫助你描述蓋子、保護蓋、手柄和其他零件如何固定。",
            "en": "Screw down, screw on and screw onto help you give practical instructions about lids, covers, handles and other parts."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "自然談論錯誤和浪費時間",
            "titleEn": "Talk naturally about mistakes and wasted time",
            "zh": "screw up 可以描述犯錯或把計劃弄糟;screw around 則可以描述有人不工作,只顧胡鬧浪費時間。",
            "en": "Screw up can describe a mistake or a spoiled plan, while screw around can describe people who are wasting time instead of working."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "描述不公平的欺騙和強迫",
            "titleEn": "Describe unfair treatment and strong pressure",
            "zh": "screw somebody out of something 表示某人被騙走東西;screw something out of somebody 則表示有人在壓力或威脅下被迫交出某物。",
            "en": "Screw somebody out of something shows that someone was cheated. Screw something out of somebody shows that pressure or threats were used to obtain something."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "表達鼓起勇氣和嚴重的情緒影響",
            "titleEn": "Express courage and serious emotional effects",
            "zh": "screw up your courage 表示迫使自己鼓起勇氣行動;screw somebody up 則描述較嚴重而持久的心理影響。",
            "en": "Screw up your courage describes making yourself brave enough to act. Screw somebody up describes a much more serious and lasting emotional effect."
          }
        ],
