          "labelEn": "SIT Phrasal Verbs in Use",
          "summaryZh": "sit around 表示無所事事地消磨時間;sit by 的意思更嚴重,表示眼看不好的事情發生,卻沒有採取行動。；sit in on a meeting 表示以旁聽者身分出席;sit in for somebody 表示暫代某人;sit on acommittee 則表示擔任委員會成員。；當某人選擇不參加或被迫錯過比賽、舞蹈、旅程或其他活動時,可以使用 sit something out。；sit back、sit somebody down 和 sit somebody up 分別描述三種不同的動作或坐姿。",
          "summaryEn": "Sit around means spending time doing very little. Sit by is more serious: it means failing to act while something wrong is happening. Sit in on a meeting means attending as an observer. Sit in for somebody means replacing that person. Sit on a committee means being one of its members. Sit something out is useful when someone chooses or has to miss a game, dance, trip or other activity. Sit back, sit somebody down and sit somebody up describe three different movements or sitting positions.",
