        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "清楚區分不同形式的「不行動」",
            "titleEn": "Describe different kinds of inactivity clearly",
            "zh": "sit around 表示無所事事地消磨時間;sit by 的意思更嚴重,表示眼看不好的事情發生,卻沒有採取行動。",
            "en": "Sit around means spending time doing very little. Sit by is more serious: it means failing to act while something wrong is happening."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論會議和臨時職務",
            "titleEn": "Talk about meetings and temporary roles",
            "zh": "sit in on a meeting 表示以旁聽者身分出席;sit in for somebody 表示暫代某人;sit on acommittee 則表示擔任委員會成員。",
            "en": "Sit in on a meeting means attending as an observer. Sit in for somebody means replacing that person. Sit on a committee means being one of its members."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "表達某人是否參與活動",
            "titleEn": "Express whether someone joins an activity",
            "zh": "當某人選擇不參加或被迫錯過比賽、舞蹈、旅程或其他活動時,可以使用 sit something out。",
            "en": "Sit something out is useful when someone chooses or has to miss a game, dance, trip or other activity."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "更準確地描述身體姿勢",
            "titleEn": "Describe body position more precisely",
            "zh": "sit back、sit somebody down 和 sit somebody up 分別描述三種不同的動作或坐姿。",
            "en": "Sit back, sit somebody down and sit somebody up describe three different movements or sitting positions."
          }
        ],
